# Optional: bake your Supabase project into the build so a new device only needs
# to sign in, rather than pasting these into Settings.
#
# This repository already commits its own project in `.env.production`, so a
# deploy from here needs nothing. Use this file only to point a fork somewhere
# else: copy to `.env.local` for local builds, or add the same two names as
# repository *variables* (Settings -> Secrets and variables -> Actions ->
# Variables), which override the committed default.
#
# The anon key is designed to be public: row-level security is what keeps the
# data private, so only the signed-in owner can read their own rows. Never put
# the service_role key here — that one bypasses security entirely.

VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-anon-public-key
